---
import '../styles.css';
import Hero from '../components/hero.astro';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '') + '/';
---
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<meta name="description" content="Boundra makes domain boundaries explicit with a Rust architecture checker and schema-backed TypeScript contracts.">
<title>Boundra — Domain boundaries, defined.</title>
<link rel="icon" href={`${base}boundra-mark.svg`} type="image/svg+xml">

</head>
<body>
<a class="skip" href="#main">Skip to content</a>
<header class="shell nav"><a class="brand" href={base}><img src={`${base}boundra-mark.svg`} alt="" width="36" height="36">Boundra</a><nav aria-label="Main"><a href="#how">How it works</a><a href="#adoption">Adoption</a><a href="https://github.com/Oddmash/boundra/blob/main/docs/user-guide.md">Docs</a><a class="nav-github" href="https://github.com/Oddmash/boundra">GitHub</a></nav></header>
<main id="main">
<Hero />
<section class="proof"><div class="shell proof-grid"><div><strong>6</strong><span>boundary rules</span></div><div><strong>4</strong><span>native CLI targets</span></div><div><strong>2</strong><span>independent adoption paths</span></div></div></section>
<section id="how" class="shell section"><div class="section-head"><p class="eyebrow">HOW IT WORKS</p><h2>Structure you can verify.</h2><p>Define domains, declare allowed relationships, and check them against your source. The runtime handles schema validation at the application boundary.</p></div><div class="features"><article><span class="tag">01 / ARCHITECTURE</span><h3>Declare the boundary.</h3><p>Each domain has layer directories, public entry points and a manifest that specifies its dependencies.</p><pre><code>domains/order/
  client/
  server/
  shared/
  domain manifest</code></pre></article><article><span class="tag">02 / STATIC ANALYSIS</span><h3>Catch drift in CI.</h3><p>Report forbidden layer imports, undeclared dependencies and internal cross-domain imports.</p><pre><code>pnpm exec boundra \
  check-boundaries \
  --format json</code></pre></article><article><span class="tag">03 / CONTRACTS</span><h3>Validate both directions.</h3><p>Define input and result schemas, then connect your own transport and API implementation.</p><pre><code>{`defineQuery({
  name: "get-order",
  input: inputSchema,
  result: resultSchema
})`}</code></pre></article></div></section>
<section id="adoption" class="adoption"><div class="shell section"><div class="section-head"><p class="eyebrow">ADOPT INCREMENTALLY</p><h2>Start with one domain.</h2><p>Keep your existing framework, build, and backend. Try a single domain before expanding the policy across a repository.</p></div><div class="flow"><ol><li><b>Initialize</b><code>boundra init --name my-app</code></li><li><b>Scaffold</b><code>boundra create-domain order</code></li><li><b>Generate a contract</b><code>boundra generate query order/get-order</code></li><li><b>Check and visualize</b><code>boundra check-boundaries</code></li></ol><aside><h3>When Boundra fits</h3><p>Use it when multiple domains and entry points need consistent dependency policy. A small app or a project already well governed by Nx or ESLint may need little more.</p><h3>What it is not</h3><p>Boundra does not replace authorization, a backend framework, a bundler, or runtime integration tests. Static analysis is limited to supported source patterns and configured domains.</p><a href="https://github.com/Oddmash/boundra/blob/main/docs/product-positioning.md">Read the full trade-off analysis</a></aside></div></div></section>
<section class="shell section final"><p class="eyebrow">BUILD WITH BOUNDARIES</p><h2>Make the rules part of the codebase.</h2><p>Read the practical guide, review the example workspace, or explore the CLI specification.</p><div class="actions"><a class="primary" href="https://github.com/Oddmash/boundra/blob/main/docs/user-guide.md">User guide</a><a class="secondary" href="https://github.com/Oddmash/boundra/tree/main/examples/order-billing">Example workspace</a></div><div class="locales"><a href="https://github.com/Oddmash/boundra/blob/main/docs/user-guide.ko.md" lang="ko">한국어</a><a href="https://github.com/Oddmash/boundra/blob/main/docs/user-guide.ja.md" lang="ja">日本語</a><a href="https://github.com/Oddmash/boundra/blob/main/docs/user-guide.zh-cn.md" lang="zh-CN">简体中文</a></div></section>
</main>
<footer class="shell footer"><a class="brand" href={base}><img src={`${base}boundra-mark.svg`} alt="" width="28" height="28">Boundra</a><span>Built by <a href="https://github.com/Oddmash">Oddmash</a> · MIT</span><a href="https://www.npmjs.com/package/boundra">npm</a></footer>
</body>
</html>
